<title>JAPAN: Kyoei Life boosts reserves to cover bad loan loss.</title>
<headline>Kyoei Life boosts reserves to cover bad loan loss.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kyoei Life Insurance Co Ltd said on Thursday that it had completed boosting its loan loss reserves to cover expected losses from bad loans.</p>
<p>The company expects that losses from bad loans will total 33.8 billion yen.</p>
<p>The insurer also said during its earnings announcement that it would invest an extra 60 billion yen in foreign bonds in the second half of the current business year to March 31.</p>
</text>
